  "id": "COMPOUND:22287 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Astersaponin F appears to interact with Replicase polyprotein 1ab through a shared target of multiple compounds, namely Dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinase. This kinase is a common target for Astersaponin F, Javanicoside F, and Ascidiathiazone B, all of which in turn target Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The evidence suggests a potential mechanism where Astersaponin F may inhibit the kinase, thereby reducing the activity of Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The overlapping targets imply a possible functional relationship, though the exact mechanism of Astersaponin F's interaction with the kinase remains to be elucidated. The consistent targeting of Replicase polyprotein 1ab by multiple compounds supports a role in the pathogenesis of the disease, though further studies are needed to confirm the precise molecular pathway.",
